            <ArticleTitle>Alkyl radical triggered in situ SO2-capture cascades.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>13324-13327</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c7cc08362a</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>An unprecedented in situ SO2-capture cascade triggered by alkyl radicals has been documented herein. Mechanistic investigations suggest that, triggered by alkyl radicals, SO2 was released in situ and subsequently fixed into polycyclic small molecules. A wide range of alkylsulfonyl substituted polycyclic compounds were easily prepared with high yields and good functional group tolerability.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
